    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Depth-first, reverse traversal for edges.</para><para>This traversal follows edges in their reverse order from target to source visiting child edges before siblings. The advancing methods and operators (<ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1_1GraphTraversal_1a574c3e3db87c283066fd908ef4ab0863" kindref="member">advance</ref>, <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1_1GraphEdgeTraversal_1a511c08698e8727dc14d9e63831fd3c52" kindref="member">next</ref>, etc.) stop only at edge enter events (<ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1a4a563d6bb47e082bbe1e40bcc59e1f59a0959fa465db7d4309420127156f68225" kindref="member">ENTER_EDGE</ref>). Dereferencing the traversal object returns a graph edge node. </para>    </detaileddescription>
